{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:wedge-covectors","title":"def:wedge-covectors","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":1388,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#def:wedge-covectors","uses":[],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"def:wedge-covectors","line":2358,"source":"\\begin{definition}[The Wedge Product of Covectors]\n\\label{def:wedge-covectors}\n\n\n\n\nFor continuous linear functionals $f_1,\\ldots,f_n$ on a real topological vector space, define\n\\[\n(f_1\\wedge\\cdots\\wedge f_n)(v_1,\\ldots,v_n)=\\det\\bigl(f_i(v_j)\\bigr)_{i,j=1}^n.\n\\]\nThis determinant convention yields a continuous alternating $n$-form.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[The Wedge Product of Covectors] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a77656467652d636f766563746f7273\"></span> <p></p>For continuous linear functionals <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f_1,\\ldots ,f_n$\">$f_1,\\ldots ,f_n$</span> on a real topological vector space, define <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  (f_1\\wedge \\cdots \\wedge f_n)(v_1,\\ldots ,v_n)=\\det \\bigl(f_i(v_j)\\bigr)_{i,j=1}^n.  \\]\">\\[  (f_1\\wedge \\cdots \\wedge f_n)(v_1,\\ldots ,v_n)=\\det \\bigl(f_i(v_j)\\bigr)_{i,j=1}^n.  \\]</span> This determinant convention yields a continuous alternating <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$n$\">$n$</span>-form. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:top-forms-proportional","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:volume-form-coframe","relations":[],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"r